# Git and environments (user decision 2026-10-22)

Full rules: `docs/agents/git-workflow.md`.

- GitHub holds exactly two branches: `dev` (test site) and `main` (production). Never push or open a PR from any other branch. Never push or merge `main`. Never force-push. Never delete `dev`.
- Flow: verify locally (`scripts/verify.sh`) → land on `dev` (`scripts/land.sh`, fast-forward only) → the user tests the dev site → the user merges the single release PR `dev → main`.
- Push only verified work: every push is a Vercel deployment and the Hobby plan allows about 100 a day. GitHub Actions is failing on account billing, so local verification is the gate.
- Check `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/dev HEAD` before rebasing. If true, do not rebase. Otherwise use `git rebase --rebase-merges origin/dev`.
- Local servers: web on port 3000, engine on port 8000, nothing else (`scripts/local-app.sh`). If busy, wait for the owner; never pick another port; stop what you start.
- Children never push or open PRs; the parent lands.
